      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of the number 24, we start by finding its prime factorization. We begin by dividing 24 by the smallest prime number, which is 2:\n\n\\[\n24 \\div 2 = 12\n\\]\n\nNext, we divide 12 by 2:\n\n\\[\n12 \\div 2 = 6\n\\]\n\nWe continue dividing by 2:\n\n\\[\n6 \\div 2 = 3\n\\]\n\nFinally, 3 is a prime number, so we stop here. Thus, the prime factorization of 24 is:\n\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\n\nTo find the number of positive divisors, we use the formula for the number of divisors based on the prime factorization. If a number \\( n \\) has a prime factorization of \\( p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\), then the number of positive divisors of \\( n \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\n\\]\n\nFor \\( 24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\), the exponents are 3 and 1. Applying the formula:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of positive divisors of 24 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we list all the positive divisors of 24: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, and 24. There are indeed 8 divisors. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
